<code>assert \old(this.get(index)).equals(oldValue);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \old(this.get(index)).equals(oldValue);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert Objects.checkIndex(index, size) => \result.equals(oldValue);</code>

However, since `Objects.checkIndex(index, size)` throws an exception if the index is invalid, we don't need to include it in the condition. Instead, we can directly assert that the returned value is the element that was at that position before the update:

<code>assert \result.equals(oldValue);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \result.equals(oldValue);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \result.equals(\old(this.get(index)));</code>
--------------------
